Let $z = 4 - \sqrt{3} + (-1 - 4 \sqrt{3})i.$  A $120^\circ$ rotation around the origin in the clockwise direction is equivalent to multiplying by $e^{-i \pi/3} = \cos (-\pi/3) + i \sin (-\pi/3) = \cos \pi/3 - i \sin \pi/3 = \frac{1}{2} - \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} i.$  Therefore, the resulting complex number is
\begin{align*} z \left( \frac{1}{2} - \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} i \right) &= (4 - \sqrt{3} + (-1 - 4 \sqrt{3})i) \left( \frac{1}{2} - \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} i \right) \\ &= (4 - \sqrt{3}) \left( \frac{1}{2} \right) + (-1 - 4 \sqrt{3}) \left( -\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} \right) + \left[ (4 - \sqrt{3}) \left( -\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} \right) + (-1 - 4 \sqrt{3}) \left( \frac{1}{2} \right) \right] i \\ &= \frac{4 - \sqrt{3}}{2} + \frac{\sqrt{3} + 12}{2} + \left[ -\frac{4 \sqrt{3} - 3}{2} - \frac{1 + 4 \sqrt{3}}{2} \right] i \\ &= \frac{4 - \sqrt{3} + \sqrt{3} + 12}{2} + \left[ \frac{-4 \sqrt{3} + 3 - 1 - 4 \sqrt{3}}{2} \right] i \\ &= \frac{16}{2} + \left[ \frac{-8 \sqrt{3} + 2}{2} \right] i \\ &= 8 + (-4 \sqrt{3} + 1) i \\ &= 8 + (1 - 4 \sqrt{3}) i. \end{align*}

Final Answer: The final answer is $\boxed{8 + (1 - 4 \sqrt{3})i}$

